Subject: [PATCH 09727/11362] [outer-loop] Per-attempt world-model retention
 (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6690)

The live engine store is keyed by game only, so every re-induction
overwrote the previous model. Measured: 40 attempts -> 25 surviving
files on the 2026-08-22 baseline run (15 models destroyed); 355
committed store versions across 27 files survive only as git
archaeology. project_arc_engine_store_regression recorded the same
defect on 2026-07-29 (ka59 fidelity 1.0 -> 0.0).

Fix shape (lowest scored-path risk of the three considered): the
canonical world_model.py write is UNCHANGED byte-for-byte; every
producer write is additionally archived under
E3_DIR/<game>/attempts/ (content-hash dedup + append-only
manifest.jsonl). Keep-best-at-write lost because no fidelity signal
exists at write time (it would silently become keep-last), and
REQ-ARC-WMTE-6035 already selects best-per-loop above this layer.
A version-keyed canonical path lost because it changes the read
contract of load_engine -- a real scored-path behaviour change.

Restore sites (_retain_engine_source_on_disk, _restore_engine_store)
deliberately do not archive: they write back content a producer site
already archived. Fail-open past the test-guard, stated in the
docstring; kill switch CARNOT_ARC_ENGINE_ATTEMPT_ARCHIVE=0.

Evidence: 14 tests (SCENARIO-6690-1..6), 10 mutations M1-M10 each
RED then restored byte-identical, final GREEN. On/off equivalence
asserted on (ok, msg, canonical bytes). During mutation M6 the
guard-deleted mutant wrote untracked results/arc_e3/gme/attempts/
-- cleaned, and the guard test now aims at a stand-in tracked dir
so a broken guard can never write real evidence again.

Note: the bulk of this change was swept into conductor commit
99fdf2797e by its auto-commit while in flight; this commit carries
the ruff UP017 fix and the spec Implementation Status fill.

Pre-existing failures NOT from this change (verified identical at
99fdf2797e~1 in a throwaway worktree): 8 failures in
test_codeonly_induce_scoping.py + test_induce_split_fallback.py.

